      "content": "\"somatic memory\" sounds interesting. i think we should lean into that to explain the energy transfer. if we can argue that my current neurological hyper-sensitivity is the same \"signal\" that was being misinterpreted as tremors back then, it would prove the physical link. i have some raw EEG data from my latest session that shows a very specific frequency spike during high-focus tasks—it's almost identical to how the physician described his \"manic bursts\" of productivity. \n\ncan you help me refine the language so it sounds scientifically rigorous rather than just speculative? i need to present this to the society as a formal biological proof of identity through temporal resonance, not just a theory. how should we structure the data presentation to make it undeniable to them?",
